div.div:
ĕpistȳlĭum ,
			ii, n., = ἐπιστύλιον, in arch., 
I.the cross-beam that rests on the
			columns, the architrave, Vitr. 3, 1
				sq.; 4, 3;
				5, 1; Varr.
				R. R. 3, 5, 11; Plin. 36, 14, 21, § 96;
			cf. Paul. ex Fest. p. 82, 11 Müll.
					Isid. Orig. 15, 8, 15;
				19, 10, 24; Vulg. 3 Reg. 7, 6 al.
